A room can be lit or unlit. The Kitchen is a room. The Kitchen is lit.

Chapter 2 - Life in the Age of Anarchy

[Carry out an actor burning (this is the carry out burning rule): now the noun is nowhere.
Report an actor burning (this is the report burning rule): say "[The actor] burns [the noun]."]
	
Book 3 - Scene Definitions

[Section 1 - More Comments

The following is a commented out section with rules and code:

Burning is an action applying to one thing.
Understand "burn [something]" as burning.

Check burning:
	if the noun is fireproof:
		say "[The noun] cannot be burned." instead;
	
Carry out burning:
	now the noun is nowhere;
	
Report burning:
	say "You burn [the noun] to ashes."]

Book 4 - Active Rules

Instead of jumping:
	say "You jump on the spot.";
	
Carry out an actor examining a container (this is the standard examining containers rule):
	if the noun is open:
		say "[The noun] contains [a list of things in the noun]." 